From b94dabf1b0bae0bdb77d309947a6847244f863f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 20:26:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/mdp5: check both ownership maps for the right pipe

The two-pipe search checks old and new ownership for the left pipe,
but accepts the next matching right pipe without checking either map.
It can overwrite another plane's assignment or reuse a pipe released
only in the current transaction, contrary to the allocator's existing
restriction on immediate reuse.

Apply the same two-map exclusion to each right-pipe candidate before
checking type and priority. Preserve allocation failure when fewer than
two eligible pipes remain.

An actual-source model enumerates all 256 eight-pipe occupancy masks
in old-only, new-only, mixed and released-in-new transactions. Combined
with the cached-state tests, 1258 cases pass 20150 checks under address,
undefined-behavior and leak sanitizers. The original allocator fails;
controls dropping either map check fail as well. ARM/ARM64 complete
MSM components build with W=1 and no compiler diagnostics.

Codex (GPT-6) found and prepared this fix while qualifying the MDP5
plane-state port. Synthetic core/lock/SMP services are used; physical
source-split scanout and concurrent DRM commits are not established.
This is a local unsigned draft for human review, with no agent DCO.

Fixes: b14892801078 ("drm/msm/mdp5: Update mdp5_pipe_assign to spit out both planes")
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6

Backport this exact delta to the maintained 6.18.63 Fx0 tree. Its
existing cached-ownership and encoder-flush fixes are preserved.
The LTS actual-source ownership model passes 1258 cases and 20150
checks; the baseline fails 1052 assertions. Five behavioral controls
fail without sanitizer diagnostics. Core locks, PM and SMP are modeled;
physical resume and the earlier r2 display fault remain unqualified.

The combined LTS series compiles six selected MDP5, IOMMU and input
objects per profile: ARM normal, ARM64 normal and ARM64 RT. All three
verify nonpermissive CFI, with W=1 and no diagnostics. ARM32 RT is
unsupported by this LTS and is not counted. These object checks do
not qualify a full link, package update or hardware operation.

Codex prepared this local backport and verification. Human review and
DCO remain pending. No publication or maintainer contact is authorized.

Backported from commit 68bc7d6951bfe79e84e6fbea4f9297f34f2d57ee
("drm/msm/mdp5: check both ownership maps for the right pipe")
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_pipe.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_pipe.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_pipe.c
index 99b2c30b1d48..b029652486f5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_pipe.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_pipe.c
@@ -66,6 +66,11 @@ int mdp5_pipe_assign(struct drm_atomic_state *s, struct drm_plane *plane,
 					struct mdp5_hw_pipe *r_cur =
 							mdp5_kms->hwpipes[j];
 
+					/* Both halves must be free in both states. */
+					if (new_state->hwpipe_to_plane[r_cur->idx] ||
+					    old_state->hwpipe_to_plane[r_cur->idx])
+						continue;
+
 					/* reject different types of hwpipes */
 					if (r_cur->caps != cur->caps)
 						continue;
